From: Hybrid PIVCO/traditional-Huffman decoder — STASHED, work-in-progress
Date: 2026-04-27
Apply with: git apply --3way extras/hybrid_decoder.diff
            (from repo root: extras/hybrid_decoder.diff)

This patch was extracted from a working tree on 2026-04-27 to unblock
unrelated AVX2/Zen3 perf experiments that were being confounded by the
hybrid path's `avg_steps > 2.8` threshold sending most real-text
distributions through the traditional decoder.

What it does:
  - Adds `pivco_huffman_table_t::use_traditional` flag, set in
    `pivco_huffman_build_table` when the expected tree-walk cost
    `avg_steps > 2.8`.
  - When the flag is set, all encode/decode dispatchers
    (pivco_huffman.c, _neon.c, _scalar.c) bypass PIVCO and call
    `trad_huffman_{encode,decode}_4s` instead.
  - Updates the trad_4s wire format to a length-prefixed header
    (so the decoder can return `*consumed` from a stream-of-blocks
    container).

Status when stashed:
  - Build + tests passed.
  - The 2.8 threshold was empirically too aggressive: bell_s10/bell_s30,
    prose_pride, html_wiki, source_c, json_api, log_apache, chinese_text
    all fall through to traditional, which on Zen 3 measured at ~170
    M/s — much slower than PIVCO's normal tree-walk (~700-900 M/s on
    those distributions).  Threshold tuning + per-platform calibration
    likely needed before this can ship.
  - Includes a debug `printf` in `compute_pivco_cost` block of
    huffman_table.c that should be removed before shipping.
  - Stream format change in traditional_huffman.c (header now stores
    `total_bytes` so the decoder can return `*consumed`).  Old
    trad_4s-encoded streams won't decode with the new code; this is
    not a problem within a single bench run but matters if streams
    are persisted.

What this patch does NOT touch (intentionally left in tree):
  - Instrumentation hooks (`pivco_instrument_node_size`,
    `pivco_dump_node_size_hist` declarations + implementation in
    src/pivco_instrumentation.c) — these are independent of the
    hybrid decoder and stay as work-in-progress.
  - AVX-512 vector-tail partition optimization in
    src/pivco_huffman_avx512.c — unrelated to hybrid; uses the
    `partition_32` masked variant for the < 32 element remainder.

---

